virglrenderer: a GL error while a draw is set up skips the draw

What: right before each GL draw call (and compute dispatch) vrend asks the GL
for errors. Any error means the GL refused a call while vrend set up the draw
(an attribute format, a buffer range, a binding), so older state is still in
place: the draw is skipped and logged like any GL error after a command (three
lines per context). Out of memory, a lost GL context and the "lose" policy stop
the context as before. Draws that the GL itself refuses later still only show in
the check after the command.
Why: the range checks look at what the guest asked for. When the GL refuses part
of it, the GPU uses whatever was bound before, which the checks never saw. The
format and alignment checks close the cases known today; this catches the rest.
Without it the after-command check (virgl-gl-error-skip-command.patch) let the
draw run on the stale state and only then logged the error, so a guest could
repeat it at will.
Depends on: virgl-gl-error-skip-command.patch, virgl-uniform-buffer-checks.patch.
Upstream: needs the error-skip behaviour first; not sent.
Tests: Tests/virgl/gl-oracle.c aborts when a GL draw call finds a GL error
pending, so test-gpu-ranges and every fuzz input check it.
--- a/src/vrend/vrend_renderer.c
+++ b/src/vrend/vrend_renderer.c
@@ -6746,6 +6746,19 @@
    } else {
       glDrawRangeElements(mode, d->min_index, d->max_index, d->count, elsz, indices);
    }
+}
+
+/* Right before a GL draw call or dispatch. A GL error now means the GL refused a call
+ * that set the draw up (an attribute format, a buffer range, a binding) and kept older
+ * state, which the range checks never saw: the draw is skipped. The errors count and are
+ * logged like those after a command; out of memory or a lost GL context stop the
+ * context. A draw the GL refuses itself shows up at the next draw or after the command. */
+static bool vrend_draw_state_ok(struct vrend_context *ctx)
+{
+   unsigned gl_errors = ctx->gl_errors;
+
+   return vrend_check_no_error_contained(ctx, "the state of a draw") &&
+          ctx->gl_errors == gl_errors;
 }
 
 int vrend_draw_vbo(struct vrend_context *ctx,
@@ -6974,7 +6987,7 @@
       glEnable(GL_BLEND);
    }
 
-   for (uint32_t i = 0; i < num_draws; i++)
+   for (uint32_t i = 0; i < num_draws && vrend_draw_state_ok(ctx); i++)
       vrend_issue_direct_draw(sub_ctx, info, &draws[i]);
    if (draws != &one_draw)
       free(draws);
@@ -7093,6 +7106,9 @@
    else
       glBindBuffer(GL_DISPATCH_INDIRECT_BUFFER, 0);
 
+   if (!vrend_draw_state_ok(ctx))
+      return;
+
